   313	
   314	## Backup Command Artifact
   315	
   316	The production backup command lives at
   317	`deploy/operations/backup-database.sh` with the runbook in
   318	`deploy/operations/README.md`. It references the deployed
   319	`/usr/local/bin/yalla-api` and `/usr/local/bin/yalla-worker` binaries for
   320	version coupling and service checks, but it keeps backup production outside
   321	the Yalla Go processes. The operator command invokes
   322	`pg_dump --format=custom --no-acl --no-owner --compress=9` against the
   323	least-privilege Postgres role supplied in `/etc/yalla/control-plane.env`.
   324	
   325	The command loads runtime configuration from `/etc/yalla/control-plane.env`
   326	or `YALLA_CONTROL_PLANE_ENV_FILE`. It never checks in or prints database URLs,
   327	signing keys, secret-encryption keys, Dokploy endpoints, Dokploy tokens, API
   328	keys, cookies, backup bucket credentials, or rendered environment values;
   329	`--dry-run` prints only command shape plus redacted `YALLA_*` variable names.
   330	The backup directory is operator-managed encrypted storage. The status file
   331	named by `YALLA_BACKUP_STATUS_FILE` is updated atomically with `mktemp` and
   332	`mv` only after `pg_dump` succeeds, so `/healthz/backup` never observes a
   333	partial timestamp.
   334	
   335	Before and after a backup, operators verify `/healthz`, `/readyz`, and
   336	`/healthz/backup`; the API renders stable `yalla.output.v1` or
   337	`yalla.error.v1` envelopes for those probes. Structured JSON logs from
   338	`yalla-api` and `yalla-worker` remain diagnostics only and must not contain
   339	backup credentials or rendered environment values.
   340	
   341	CI pins the command, runbook, and release gate with
   342	`go test ./internal/release/... -run TestBackupCommand`.
   343	
   344	## TLS Termination and Proxy Header Trust
   345	
   346	The Yalla control-plane API binary (`cmd/yalla-api`) deliberately
   347	does NOT terminate TLS itself.
   348	**TLS is terminated at the operator's reverse proxy**
   349	(ingress controller, load balancer, or front-door proxy), which
   350	forwards the request to the API over an internal network. Keeping certificate material out of the API process
   351	narrows the secret surface, leverages the proxy's vetted cipher
   352	suite / HSTS / OCSP stapling defaults, and lets operators rotate
   353	certificates without an API restart. The posture is pinned by
   354	`internal/release/http_server_hardening_static_test.go`; a regression
   355	in any one of the following is caught at build time:
   356	
   357	- **No in-process TLS.** The API binary MUST NOT call
   358	  `ListenAndServeTLS` or `ServeTLS`, and the constructed
   359	  `*http.Server` MUST NOT set `TLSConfig` or `TLSNextProto`. Any
   360	  TLS-termination shape inside the binary is rejected.

